-- MBL Season XII, World Series Game 5: Hershey Otters 0, Philadelphia Panthers 1.
--
-- Played 11 October 2026, umpired by alexc18 and wobber, and scored on a
-- Google Sheet rather than on this site - the same gap `import-umpire-cards`
-- papers over for the MCBA, now reaching the MBL's own final. One game, so it
-- is written out here rather than given a parser.
--
-- The Panthers take the series 4-1. Games 6 and 7 are marked NOT_NEEDED at the
-- bottom, the way this season already marks the two unplayed games of the
-- Panthers-Grizzlies series.
--
-- Every figure on the card appears twice - once in the cells, once in a totals
-- row - and all of them agreed, which is rare enough to be worth recording.
-- Both sides' hits, strikeouts, walks and home runs reconcile against the
-- other side's pitching line; the position changes, read with their out
-- counts, reproduce all five pitchers' innings exactly; and the nine men on
-- the field account for every out of every half-inning. The card settles one
-- thing the cells leave open on their own: EthanS22 left in the top of the
-- fifth "at 2 outs", which could mean before or after IcedFlxme's single, and
-- his line of 4 hits says after.
--
-- The score is the opposing pitchers' earned and unearned runs, which is the
-- one figure the cells do not carry. Only one run was scored in the game -
-- joshygg's home run in the bottom of the fifth - and the Panthers never
-- batted in the sixth, which is why their line score is a column shorter.
--
-- Two decisions the card does not name, settled by the league:
--
--   * The win is joshygg's. He came in during the top of the fifth and the
--     Panthers took the lead in the bottom of it, on his own home run, so he
--     is the pitcher of record. The loss needed no deciding - xx6tttsahur7xx
--     gave that home run up.
--   * The save is peejamillion's, for finishing a one-run game. The same
--     standard gave joshygg a save in Game 4.
--
-- "exho" on the card is Rebtsuna. It is a nickname that appears nowhere in the
-- database, and he is the only man in the Panthers' line-up it could not be
-- read off a roster for; the league named him. Nothing else needed asking -
-- every other nickname here matches a username on one of the two clubs.
--
-- Putouts are left null rather than zero. The card has no column for them, and
-- writing zeros would say thirty-three fly balls were caught by nobody.
--
-- Safe to run twice: the box score and line score are deleted before they are
-- inserted, and every season line is set to a value rather than added to - the
-- lesson of 0097, where a retried increment gave a pitcher two wins in a
-- season he pitched one. The season totals below are the existing line plus
-- this game, with every rate re-derived exactly as `recomputeSeason` derives
-- it, so recomputing Season XII Playoffs afterwards writes the same numbers
-- back rather than changing anything.

